Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Korean facility trainer speech
Applies after 0073-korean-frontier-banned-list.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

Korean build only (GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_KOREAN): the Battle Frontier's
and the Battle Tents' trainers say the Korean ROM's own sentences, as that
ROM's code has them, instead of six Easy Chat words joined in English order.
tools/localize_korean.py writes them from the player's ROM to
src/data/battle_frontier/korean_trainer_speech.h.

diff --git a/src/battle_tower.c b/src/battle_tower.c
--- a/src/battle_tower.c
+++ b/src/battle_tower.c
@@ -1916,8 +1916,61 @@
     }
 }
 
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_KOREAN
+// The Korean ROM's sentences for its facility trainers (before the battle,
+// after winning it, after losing it: three a trainer), which its own code
+// shows instead of the Easy Chat words. Read from the player's ROM by
+// tools/localize_korean.py.
+#include "data/battle_frontier/korean_trainer_speech.h"
+
+// The sentence for a speech of the facility's trainer table, or NULL (an
+// e-Reader trainer, a record-mixed one: their words are the player's).
+static const u8 *KoreanTrainerSpeech(const u16 *words)
+{
+    static const struct {
+        const struct BattleFrontierTrainer *trainers;
+        const u8 *const *speech;
+        u16 count;
+    } sTables[] = {
+        {gBattleFrontierTrainers, sKoreanFrontierSpeech, ARRAY_COUNT(sKoreanFrontierSpeech) / 3},
+        {gSlateportBattleTentTrainers, sKoreanSlateportTentSpeech, ARRAY_COUNT(sKoreanSlateportTentSpeech) / 3},
+        {gVerdanturfBattleTentTrainers, sKoreanVerdanturfTentSpeech, ARRAY_COUNT(sKoreanVerdanturfTentSpeech) / 3},
+        {gFallarborBattleTentTrainers, sKoreanFallarborTentSpeech, ARRAY_COUNT(sKoreanFallarborTentSpeech) / 3},
+    };
+    u32 i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_COUNT(sTables); i++)
+    {
+        const u8 *base = (const u8 *)sTables[i].trainers;
+        u32 offset = (const u8 *)words - base, trainer, field;
+
+        if ((const u8 *)words < base || offset >= sTables[i].count * sizeof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer))
+            continue;
+        trainer = offset / sizeof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer);
+        field = offset % sizeof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer);
+        if (field == offsetof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer, speechBefore))
+            return sTables[i].speech[trainer * 3];
+        if (field == offsetof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer, speechWin))
+            return sTables[i].speech[trainer * 3 + 1];
+        if (field == offsetof(struct BattleFrontierTrainer, speechLose))
+            return sTables[i].speech[trainer * 3 + 2];
+        return NULL;
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+#endif
+
 void FrontierSpeechToString(const u16 *words)
 {
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_KOREAN
+    const u8 *sentence = KoreanTrainerSpeech(words);
+
+    if (sentence != NULL)
+    {
+        StringCopy(gStringVar4, sentence);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     ConvertEasyChatWordsToString(gStringVar4, words, 3, 2);
     if (GetStringWidth(FONT_NORMAL, gStringVar4, -1) > 204u)
     {
